uthored `response:` is refused as ESS-AUTHOR-001, while a silent `accepts: nothing` outcome checks no returned value. A reproducer is retained in ER `ess/reproducers/pure-return/`. This work is independent of the parked ESS evolution program.\n\n## Scope\n\nExtend the existing typed command-response observation boundary with authored direct value assertions, checked against the source command response type, and automatic response shape checks where declared. Preserve old canonical bytes and readers; admit the new observation only in a new scenario/suite format. An old reader must refuse it before target callbacks. Rust runner must compare actual SemanticCommandResult.response from the exact invocation, without requiring or manufacturing an event, a persistent subject, or a query view.\n\nTyped declarations already exist: command response Field, SemanticCommandResult.response, and response::Observation; this adds observation of existing nouns, not a new runtime entity.\n\n## Acceptance scenarios\n\n- pure_return_correct_literal_passes_without_events\n- pure_return_wrong_literal_fails_named_scenario\n- pure_return_absent_field_and_extra_field_refuse\n- pure_return_unknown_response_coordinate_refuses_at_compile\n- pure_return_old_formats_refuse_before_target_effects\n- pure_return_legacy_suite_bytes_unchanged\n- pure_return_complete_nested_values_preserve_order_and_duplicates\n\nUse existing admitted suite and report/2 paths. Add a minimal design, compatibility tests, and run format, conformance crate tests and Clippy plus touched CLI checks. No Go/TypeScript runtime code is introduced: if those producers cannot execute the new construct, they must refuse generation explicitly. Binary64 remains explicitly unsupported in native ESS typed conformance pending its own governed extension; do not silently relax its admission.\n","document":{"events":[{"args":{"command":"create-entity","data":{"body":"# Direct library return observations\n\n## Accepted request and evidence\n\